  "description_html": "The \"dromaeo-avemorphs\", as they are informally known (Paul, 2002), represent a group of early paravian theropods with asymmetrical feathers and an <i>Archaeopteryx</i>-like body. According to Hartman <i>et al</i>. (2019), the animals shown in this image might, together, form a clade (monophyletic group) without modern birds.",
